    "question": {
      ":question/id": "c466701b-3279-578c-89cd-2f04b0d60255",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
      ":question/problem": "Simplify.\n\n$$\n\\left(\\sin\\left(67^\\circ\\right)-\\cos\\left(67^\\circ\\right)\\right)^2\n$$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Put $x=67^\\circ$. Expand the square and combine the squared terms.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n(\\sin x-\\cos x)^2 &=\\sin^2 x-2\\sin x\\cos x+\\cos^2 x \\\\ &=1-2\\sin x\\cos x \\\\ &=1-\\sin(2x)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHere $\\sin^2 x+\\cos^2 x=1$ and $2\\sin x\\cos x=\\sin(2x)$.\n\nSubstitute $x=67^\\circ$ and double the whole angle: $2x=134^\\circ$. The result is\n\n$$\n1-\\sin\\left(134^\\circ\\right) .\n$$",
